  "prefLabel": "En 1011.12 Operation",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 1011.12 Operation. Upon the utility’s receipt of proof of the electric code official’s approval, an interconnecting customer may begin interconnected operation of a facility, provided there is an IA in effect, the facility has passed any facility review and witness test that may be required by the utility, and the facility had received permission to operate. Evidence of approval by an electric code official shall include a signed certificate of completion or other inspector-provided documentation.\n\nSource. #14657, eff 9-1-26, EXPIRES: 9-1-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en1000.html"
